    "note": "The Lakeside Medical Center, designed by Harold Stoner in 1941 — a futuristic Streamline Moderne commercial building with glass blocks, a vertically projecting tower, curved and stepped surfaces, coping and a sign of individual letters. The statement calls it a rare intact example of a highly unique commercial building in the style, eligible for individual consideration under Criterion C/3."
